# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# CoreLogger/Sitar output (see log_viewer/README.md): <hex file's own
# basename>.log for the architectural trace, sitar.log for Sitar's own
# lower-level log, wherever they land, including the repo root when a
# model's binary is run from here as its example commands show
*.log

# Committed exceptions, the test_simple_ADD reference traces (see
# validation/README.md). Tracked at the exact path each model actually
# writes to when built and run from its own folder
# (`test_simple_ADD.log`, named after the hex file, see
# each configuration's own src/sparc_sim.cpp's traceFileName()), so
# building and running there updates the tracked file directly, nothing
# to manually copy or keep in sync.
!/model/system_models/core_only/cpp_model/test_simple_ADD.log
!/model/system_models/core_only/sitar_model/test_simple_ADD.log

# validation/test_simple_ADD/ and log_viewer/ don't keep their own copies,
# they symlink to the two tracked files above (see validation/README.md
# and log_viewer/README.md), but the symlinks themselves still need
# their own exceptions, same *.log name, same rule.
!/validation/test_simple_ADD/test_simple_ADD.cpp_model.log
!/validation/test_simple_ADD/test_simple_ADD.sitar_model.log
!/log_viewer/test_simple_ADD.log

# mkdocs build resolves log_viewer/'s symlink into a real file at this
# path, same reasoning as the log_viewer/ exception above.
!/docs/generated_site/log_viewer/test_simple_ADD.log

# MkDocs (docs/.venv/); docs/generated_site/ IS committed, not ignored
.venv/
**/*.egg-info/
